WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.029
So President elect Joe Biden is starting to
fill out his cabinet.

00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:08.850
And we learned just in the last few hours,
really, that Joe Biden, secretary of state,

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.020
is going to be Anthony Blinken.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:15.380
And you are going to notice, as I tell you
about Anthony Blinken, that this is going

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:18.890
to be very, very different than Donald Trump's
approach.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:27.269
Donald Trump's two secretaries of state were
an oil executive and a right wing nut, Congressman

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:31.810
Rex Tillerson and Mike Pompeo, respectively,
as secretaries of state.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:37.620
Joe Biden is going to have a former deputy
secretary of state who started his career

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:43.250
at the State Department under the Clinton
administration has huge foreign policy experience

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:50.620
and quite frankly, is what you need temperamentally
when you want to sort of calm the panic of

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.320
our foreign allies.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:57.850
After four years of a child in the White House
with their sycophants following them around

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.690
until they are no longer sycophants.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:02.300
Rex Tillerson, of course, being an example
of that.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:08.050
Now, this doesn't mean we're going to agree
with every cabinet pick that Joe Biden makes

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:09.050
on policy.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.540
And we're going to talk about that in a little
bit.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:15.080
But we are starting to actually select experienced
adults here, and that's a good sign.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.900
We've also learned of two more choices for
Joe Biden.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:21.460
They are Jake Sullivan for national security
adviser.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.930
Sullivan was Joe Biden's national security
adviser as VP and also worked under Hillary

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:29.530
Clinton when she was secretary of state.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.990
And then lastly, from what we know so far,
we heard about Ronald Klain a couple of weeks

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.420
ago, his chief of staff.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:40.890
The last choice I have to tell you about today
is that Linda Thomas Greenfield is going to

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.200
be Joe Biden's ambassador to the United Nations.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:49.940
Again, all important positions for rebuilding
relationships with allies.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.960
She is a 35 year foreign service veteran.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:58.850
And Biden, importantly, is going to put ambassador
to the U.N. back on the National Security

00:01:58.850 --> 00:01:59.850
Council.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:00.850
This might not seem huge.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:07.450
This is one of those things that goes sort
of to the character of how a president approaches

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:11.230
international organizations like the U.N.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:16.120
Part of Donald Trump's attacks on the United
Nations included downgrading the ambassador

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:20.250
to the U.N. so that they were no longer on
the NSC.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:25.630
Joe Biden is going to put the ambassador to
the U.N. back on the National Security Council.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:28.170
So a few thoughts so far on this.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:36.760
I'm seeing posts going around about, for example,
oh, my God, Anthony Blinken is against BDS,

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.420
the movement to boycott Israel.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.980
How dare Joe Biden?

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.720
Well, Joe Biden is against BDS.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:50.200
Who would expect that Joe Biden would pick
a secretary of state in favor of BDS if they

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.560
themselves are against BDS?

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.390
That's kind of a strange reaction to have
now a Biden.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:04.550
Blinken, rather, is Jewish and I hope that
oh my God, he's against BDS is not merely

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.040
code for oh my God, he's Jewish.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.550
I'll give the benefit of the doubt on that.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:12.530
Blinken did support the Iran deal.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:16.190
There are going to be some in Israel who don't
like that.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.780
I think the Iran deal was good.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.580
Anthony Blinken supported the Iran deal.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:24.599
I was in favor of the Iran deal, and I think
that that's a good thing.

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:31.250
Now, secondly, this now starts to give us
a sense of what the Biden foreign policy will

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:38.010
likely be with regard to foreign superpowers
as well as different regions of the world.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:42.760
We're starting to see based on these selections
of Anthony Blinken as well as Jake Sullivan,

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.879
et cetera.

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:48.260
This probably means more time, effort and
resources are going to go into the relationship

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.860
with India as an example.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:57.450
This probably means more time in Africa, where
China has spent significant time and resources

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:02.890
getting more involved with tech and infrastructure
over the last many years.

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:06.590
These are the type I mean, it feels weird
to even be talking with you guys in these

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:09.700
terms today because we're starting to get
back to policy.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:15.540
We're starting to get back to geopolitics,
foreign policy, relationships between countries.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.359
It's like this has been so sorely needed for
a long time.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:25.330
Blinken likely will also have as a priority
to spend more time trying to bolster Guatemala,

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:29.009
Honduras, El Salvador and Latin America.

00:04:29.009 --> 00:04:31.550
In what ways we don't yet know.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:37.009
And then, of course, if it's Russia, China,
Africa and Latin America, what's missing from

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:38.870
that is Middle East.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:45.150
And there may not be I mean, this may not
be an administration and a State Department

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:51.559
that is going to focus as much on the Middle
East as the recent three administrations have.

00:04:51.559 --> 00:04:55.969
That doesn't necessarily that's not necessarily
a bad thing.

00:04:55.969 --> 00:04:58.939
And of course, the devil is in the details.

00:04:58.939 --> 00:05:00.050
Trump.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:05.430
One interesting note is Donald Trump never
extended an arm controls deal with Russia,

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:09.880
and as a result of that, the incoming Biden
administration is going to have about two

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:16.169
weeks after inauguration to extend that with
Russia, if indeed it is going to be extended.

00:05:16.169 --> 00:05:17.169
That's a big thing.

00:05:17.169 --> 00:05:21.430
And that's going to set the tone for a lot
of the relaid the three way relationship between

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.379
the U.S., Russia and China.

00:05:23.379 --> 00:05:26.520
And that's going to be in the first couple
of weeks of the Biden administration.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.979
So that's something to look at.

00:05:27.979 --> 00:05:33.379
Now, there's plenty of sort of good here,
a return to normalcy, adults at the table,

00:05:33.379 --> 00:05:35.830
qualified people at the table.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.129
What's the bad?

00:05:37.129 --> 00:05:38.900
Anthony Blinken is no progressive.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.400
That's that's the reality.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:47.309
And Anthony Blinken is more interventionist
than I am, although Joe Biden has not shown

00:05:47.309 --> 00:05:53.680
an interest during the campaign in campaigning
on interventionist priorities.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:59.050
We know that Blinken is more of an interventionist
than Joe Biden ran on.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:01.199
And this is something that I'm not on board
with generally.

00:06:01.199 --> 00:06:07.229
As a rule of thumb, if you look at some of
Lincoln's past comments about Iraq seeming

00:06:07.229 --> 00:06:11.589
to be more in the mindset of the problem was
how it was done rather than the fact that

00:06:11.589 --> 00:06:13.559
it was done at all.

00:06:13.559 --> 00:06:15.699
And that's something that I disagree with.

00:06:15.699 --> 00:06:20.229
And this is the way that we are going to get
back into shifting to.

00:06:20.229 --> 00:06:21.229
OK, great.

00:06:21.229 --> 00:06:22.849
We've got adults back in charge.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:26.400
This is a highly qualified choice and that's
a good thing.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.930
But now we actually have to keep them accountable
about what they do now.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.659
One one other thing.

00:06:32.659 --> 00:06:39.159
There was a hilarious reaction from a lot
of people on the right about Biden's choosing

00:06:39.159 --> 00:06:40.159
a known name.

00:06:40.159 --> 00:06:42.830
Who the hell has ever heard of Anthony Blinken?

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:47.129
This is one of those things we're going to
have to become accustomed to after the Trump

00:06:47.129 --> 00:06:48.399
administration.

00:06:48.399 --> 00:06:54.139
Donald Trump regularly picked people because
he saw them on Fox News or saw them on TV.

00:06:54.139 --> 00:06:59.369
It's OK to have people in positions of power
that are not regulars on cable news.

00:06:59.369 --> 00:07:01.270
And that may not be household names.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.270
That's fine.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.659
And in fact, in some cases, it can be better.

00:07:04.659 --> 00:07:06.980
And I think that it's a good thing that Joe
Biden is already going in that direction.

